-# Sub-nav for the classic Rails profile settings surface. The
-# `:edit_profile` tab used to head the row — it linked back to
-# `settings_profile_path` (the same page it rendered on), so on
-# `/settings/profile` it read as a big active "Edit profile" button
-# that did nothing when clicked. Struck 2026-08-04 after Tal flagged
-# it as still-showing on the profile settings page: the page IS the
-# edit-profile page; a self-link labelled the same is redundant and
-# reads to users as if it were a call-to-action. Verification and
-# Featured hashtags remain — they're sibling sub-pages you actually
-# navigate to from here.
.content__heading__tabs
  = render_navigation renderer: :links do |primary|
    :ruby
      primary.item :verification, safe_join([material_symbol('check'), t('verification.verification')]), settings_verification_path
      primary.item :featured_tags, safe_join([material_symbol('tag'), t('settings.featured_tags')]), settings_featured_tags_path
